card.statement:
Consider the bunch of semi-chains ${\bf C}(F_3)$.

- Denote by $S$ the set of all usual strings $w$ and special strings $(w,k)$, where $w=w_0r_1w_1r_2w_2\cdots$ $r_mw_m$, such that one of the following conditions hold:

(a) $w_0=q[t-1]$, $r_1= \sim$, $w_1=z[t]$ for some $t\in \Z$ and if $w_k\in \{
x[i+1], y[i], z[i], r[i-1], p[i], q[i-1]\}$ then $i\geq t$;

(b) $w_m=q[t-1]$, $r_m= \sim$, $w_{m-1}=z[t]$ for some $t\in \Z$ and if $w_k\in \{
x[i+1], y[i], z[i], r[i-1], p[i], q[i-1]\}$ then $i\geq t$;

(c) $w_0=r[t-1]$, $r_{1}= \sim$, $w_{1}=x[t+1]$, $w_2\ne r[t+1]$ for some $t\in \Z$ and if $w_k\in \{
  x[i+1], y[i], z[i], r[i-1], p[i], q[i-1]\}$ then $i\geq t$;

(d) $w_m=r[t-1]$, $r_m= \sim$, $w_{m-1}=x[t+1]$, $w_{m-2}\ne r[t+1]$ for some $t\in \Z$ and if $w_k\in \{
x[i+1], y[i], z[i], r[i-1], p[i], q[i-1]\}$ then $i\geq t$.

- Denote by $\Psi$ the set of all $M\in {\bf Ver}\, {\rm rep}\,({\bf C}(F_3))$ which correspond to the elements from $S$.
